    "body": "## Overview\n\n`RoutedExperts.weight_loader` copied the full `w2_bias` to every TP rank, so the row-parallel down projection added it `tp_size` times before the all-reduce. Only TP rank 0 now keeps it, as gpt-oss's own loader already does. Fixes #65405.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Biased experts loaded through the generic loader are correct at TP>1. TP=1, EP (where `tp_rank` is 0 on every rank) and gpt-oss's native loader are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew test `TestLoadWeightsExpertBias::test_down_bias_owned_by_tp_rank_zero` in `tests/kernels/moe/test_moe_weight_loading_padded.py`. It builds a real `FusedMoEConfig`, `ExpertMapManager` and `RoutedExperts` for `(tp_size, tp_rank)` in `(1, 0)`, `(2, 0)`, `(2, 1)`, `(4, 3)`, loads a nonzero bias through `load_weights`, and checks that rank 0 holds the bias and every other rank holds zeros.\n\n```bash\npytest -v \"tests/kernels/moe/test_moe_weight_loading_padded.py::TestLoadWeightsExpertBias::test_down_bias_owned_by_tp_rank_zero\"\npytest -q tests/kernels/moe/test_moe_weight_loading_padded.py tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_gpt_oss_weight_loading.py \"tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_reload.py::test_padded_moe_reload_releases_each_layer\"\n```\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| New test | 2 passed, `[2-1]` and `[4-3]` failed (rank holds the full bias instead of zeros) | 4 passed |\n| Second command | 109 passed, 2 failed (same two cases), 4 skipped (CUDA only) | 111 passed, 4 skipped |\n\nEnd to end on CPU with `FusedMoEFactory(has_bias=True)`, the TP=2 and TP=4 error before the fix is exactly `(tp_size - 1)` times the bias term, and 0 after it (numbers in the linked issue).\n\nFull model on CPU through `LLM(model_impl=\"transformers\")`, fp32, eager: a tiny saved HF checkpoint (Mixtral router/attention/decoder with a `ModuleList` of biased `LlamaMLP` experts, 1 layer, 2 experts), so loading goes through `TransformersRoutedExperts` and the generic `RoutedExperts.weight_loader`. Reference is the reloaded HF model run eagerly in fp32; 3 prompts, 4 greedy tokens each.\n\n| | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| TP=1 | matches HF (first-token logprob error 2.4e-7) | matches HF (2.4e-7) |\n| TP=2 | rank 1 holds the full `w2_bias`; logprob error 2.73, greedy tokens `[4, 4, 4, 4]` instead of HF's `[3, 3, 3, 3]` | rank 1 holds zeros; matches HF (2.4e-7) |\n\nNot run: GPU, and no public pretrained checkpoint (I haven't found one with per-expert biases that loads through the Transformers backend).\n\n## Details\n\nThe check reads `moe_config.tp_rank`, the rank inside the group the down-projection all-reduce spans. With DP/PCP folded into TP that is the flattened rank. With EP, and with sequence-parallel MoE (which requires EP), `tp_rank` is 0 on every rank, so each rank keeps the bias of the experts it owns.\n\nNo open PR covers this branch (searched `w2_bias` and `moe bias tp_rank`). The open reload PRs #61287, #50523 and #65353 don't touch `routed_experts.py`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
